  title: "The Yukon: A River Road from the Company to the Klondike",
  description: "The Yukon was a Hän, Tutchone, Tagish and Gwich'in river, and a Tlingit trade road from the coast, long before the Hudson's Bay Company crept in from the Mackenzie in the 1840s or a hundred thousand stampeders poured over the Chilkoot in 1898. This lesson follows the river from the company's hungry posts to the Klondike and asks what the gold rush cost the people whose river it was.",
